{"game": "risk-of-rain-2", "language": "english", "appid": 632360, "month": "2019-12", "window": 1, "start_date": 1575158400, "end_date": 1575763199, "month_true_total": 5923, "quota": 7, "returned": 7, "pulled_at": "2026-09-13 02:42:29 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "59457554", "author": {"steamid": "76561198964088220", "personaname": "motardpdx", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198964088220/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 5, "playtime_forever": 29754, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 7078, "last_played": 1768830160, "avatar": "4faad867388980b2f1c3fb0316de39267bcd5892"}, "language": "english", "review": "fun game bro", "timestamp_created": 1575762962, "timestamp_updated": 1575762962, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1553788800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "59456532", "author": {"steamid": "76561197980449778", "personaname": "Jupiter", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/biomatter/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 58, "playtime_forever": 4115, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 3033, "last_played": 1718168231, "avatar": "6a17d8dfdff63d5a00b13bb72a7703c8f7067840"}, "language": "english", "review": "This is an early access review: I hope that the game changes to invalidate this review. I want to like it.\n\nI'll skip the highlights of the game; there are other reviews for that. My beef with the game is the way this roguelite handles itemization. You have next-to-no control over what items you'll find making success feel luck-dependent. On top of that, you inhale such a huge quantity of items over the course of a single 30 min ~ 1hr run that individual runs don't feel very unique. You'll have multiple copies of nearly every white item (the most common rarity), a broad swash of greens, and (if you're lucky) a few useful red items. It doesn't help that many items are truly useless because the devs have explicitly stated that items are tiered not by power, but how rare their effects should be. This means that there are some green and red items that completely blow for 90% of the cast's playstlye. (This applies to white items too, but again, you get so many of those it's harder to complain about them.)\n\nI really want to like this game because I was in love with the first game, but playing this game leads me to believe that I've been wearing rose-tinted lenses because I can't help but compare it to roguelites that I like more. In Binding of Isaac, you aren't swamped with upgrades or items, and many of them are so powerful you change the way you play. Same for Nuclear Throne: a small amount of upgrades that are very powerful shape your character semi-randomly. etc. etc. for other good roguelites.\n\nIn summary my complaint is that the player has almost no agency in the quality of their runs.\n\n(This is ignoring more banal complaints about balance like getting two-shot by projectiles from behind, which do exist but are more easily addressed as pure number games.)", "timestamp_created": 1575761574, "timestamp_updated": 1575761574, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.441605865955352783", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1553788800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "59454004", "author": {"steamid": "76561197970666898", "personaname": "Shr0", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/alualu/", "num_games_owned": 1162, "num_reviews": 75, "playtime_forever": 9002, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 1, "playtime_at_review": 529, "last_played": 1788381043, "avatar": "eca34061e1fba65c24f8f90de4ae832ab738c730"}, "language": "english", "review": "Pro:\n+entertaining challenge\n+starting over does not feel repetetive\n+multiplayer option is mostly fun\n+singleplayer quite addictive\n+no micropayment options\n\ncon:\n-multiplayer gets the same amount of loot, so its split by two, which is quite frustrating for everyone most of the time \n-in multiplayer the loot situation causes players to split up and greedily search for boxes so the other one doesn't take them, so people die alone all the time. \n", "timestamp_created": 1575758325, "timestamp_updated": 1575758325, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.528985500335693359", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1553788800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "59453907", "author": {"steamid": "76561198217986243", "personaname": "Random Chimp Event", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/ASleepySteamyMeatPie/", "num_games_owned": 126, "num_reviews": 9, "playtime_forever": 23766, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 20191, "last_played": 1765562410, "avatar": "2e78650ed13de6d56ede527915139bfacf1d9ed7"}, "language": "english", "review": "Worth the try if you have the spare time\n\n...As long as the idea of a third-person shooter rougelike that scales difficulty based on time sounds appealing to you.", "timestamp_created": 1575758208, "timestamp_updated": 1738314726, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.545454561710357666", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1553788800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "59453444", "author":